; kernelx.def — ERA (Xbox One) kernel import lib (phase 5).
; XMemAlloc/XMemFree are a 1:1 map to the GDK xmem.dll functions (same
; API, different module); see docs/ERA-GDK-MAPPING.md.
; Ordinals are WinDurango's kernelx.dll ordinals (dumpbin /exports
; 2026-11-23) — the only real ordinal layout available. The real FH2
; exe imports kernelx BY NAME, so its import table gives hints, not
; ordinals (exe hints: XMemAlloc 479, XMemFree 482, XMemAllocDefault
; 480, XMemFreeDefault 483, XMemSetAllocationHooks 487,
; TitleMemoryStatus 433; WinDurango ordinals: 514, 517, 515, 518, 524,
; 463). A hint is an index into the sorted export-name table, not an
; ordinal. kernelx's other imports in a real ERA title are Win32 API
; names (~106 in FH2) that the layer forwards to kernel32.dll at load
; time — they are not in this .def because they are not layer exports
; (see src/pe_loader.cpp). VirtualAlloc is the one exception to the
; forward: the layer translates it (HleVirtualAlloc, FH2 boot #2 fix
; 2026-11-23) via the HLE table, NOT via this .def — putting the NAME
; "VirtualAlloc" here would make the era guest link it from kernelx.lib
; and reroute the CRT's own VirtualAlloc calls through the wrapper
; (kernelx.lib is searched before kernel32.lib). Instead the test hook
; is exported under its own name, HleVirtualAlloc, so the era guest can
; call the wrapper directly and unit-test the flag translation while
; the guest's (and the CRT's) plain VirtualAlloc still goes to
; kernel32. The FH2 boot retry is the end-to-end proof that the real
; kernelx!VirtualAlloc import routes to HleVirtualAlloc.
LIBRARY kernelx
EXPORTS
    XMemAlloc @514
    XMemFree @517
    XMemAllocDefault @515
    XMemFreeDefault @518
    XMemSetAllocationHooks @524
    TitleMemoryStatus @463
    HleVirtualAlloc
